# URAE Mathematics Notepad: Abstract Algebra & Galois Theory
# Interactive study of polynomial splitting fields, Galois groups, quotient rings, and radical solvability.

x: Variable

# 1. Polynomial Splitting Field & Galois Group
# P(x) = x⁵ - 4x + 2 is irreducible by Eisenstein (p=2) with 3 real roots -> Gal(P) ≅ S₅ (not solvable by radicals)
poly = x^5 - 4*x + 2
galois_group(poly, x)
is_solvable_by_radicals(poly, x)

# 2. Cyclotomic Polynomials & Automorphisms
# Φ_n(x) has Galois group isomorphic to (Z/nZ)ˣ
cyclotomic_poly(n = 12, var = x)
splitting_field(x^3 - 2, x)

# 3. Finite Group Structures & Quotient Rings
G = symmetric_group(4)
group_order(G)
group_conjugacy_classes(G)
group_character_table(G)
